>> title: General Tso's Chicken
>> category: Stir-Fries
>> tags: chicken, chiles, chinese, deep-fry, wok
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: general tso, general tsos chicken, general gau, general chos chicken, C16, C12, 左宗棠雞, zuo zong tang ji
>> pairs-with: egg-fried-rice, egg-rolls
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — once the chicken is tossed in the glaze it has about a minute before the crust softens for good
>> washing-up: the wok, a bowl to velvet in, a dish to dredge in, a rack to drain on, a bowl for the glaze

>> step: velvet, rest 30 min
Toss @chicken thighs{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; boneless, cut in 1-in pieces) with @egg white{1}, @Shaoxing wine{1%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, and @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, then ~rest{30%min} in the fridge — this is the velveting, and it is why takeout chicken is tender where a plain fry is not.

>> step: dredge dry, shake off the loose
Dredge @&(~1)velveted chicken{} in @cornstarch{3/4%cup}(90 g), piece by piece, shaking off what does not cling.

>> step: fry 350°F 5 min, again at 375°F 2 min
Fry @&(~1)coated chicken{} in @peanut oil{4%cups}(950 mL) in two batches at 350°F (175°C) for ~fry{5%min}, rest them on a rack, then return every piece to the oil at 375°F (190°C) for ~fry{2%min}.

>> step: stir the glaze smooth
Stir @chicken stock{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @dark soy sauce{2%Tbs}, @sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @rice vinegar{2%Tbs}, and @cornstarch{2%tsp} smooth in a bowl.

>> step: sizzle the chiles, pour in, simmer 1 min
Sizzle @dried red chiles{8}(stemmed, whole) with @garlic{3%cloves}(minced), @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated), and @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp} in a hot #wok{} for 20 seconds, pour @&(~1)glaze{} in, and ~simmer{1%min} until it is glossy and coats a spoon.

>> step: toss to coat, serve at once
Toss @&(~3)fried chicken{} through @&(~1)glaze{} off the heat, only until every piece is coated, and serve at once — it goes soft standing in the sauce.
